# Keep systemd-networkd off the ethernet port. NetworkManager owns it.
#
# This is the mirror image of 10-unmanaged-interfaces.conf, which tells NetworkManager to
# keep off can0. That half existed; this half did not, so BOTH stacks were claiming
# enP8p1s0 -- stock /usr/lib/systemd/network/80-wired.network matches Type=ether and runs
# DHCP=yes on it, against the static 192.168.1.5/32 that static-eth.nmconnection assigns
# for the LiDAR.
#
# TWO THINGS THIS FIXES
#
# 1. TWO MINUTES OF BOOT, EVERY BOOT. Measured on the unit 2026-08-17:
#
#        systemd-analyze blame  ->  2min 257ms systemd-networkd-wait-online.service
#        systemctl is-failed    ->  failed
#
#    A link networkd manages is Required For Online by default. With no cable in the LiDAR
#    port enP8p1s0 sits at no-carrier (configuring) forever, so wait-online burned its full
#    120 s timeout and then failed. It was the single largest item in `systemd-analyze
#    blame`. (can0 was the other blocker, for a different reason -- see can0.network.)
#
# 2. A LATENT SSH-KILLER. Read the trap list at the top of static-eth.nmconnection: a /24
#    or a default route on this interface beats WiFi on metric and takes SSH to the box
#    with it, recoverable only over serial. A DHCP client that networkd was free to run
#    here could install exactly that. It has not bitten yet only because the Livox is a
#    sensor, not a DHCP server, so the lease request goes unanswered -- i.e. we are relying
#    on there being no DHCP server on that cable. Plug this port into a real network once
#    and that stops being true.
#
# Unmanaged=yes rather than RequiredForOnline=no: the latter would fix the boot time alone
# and leave networkd still configuring an interface NetworkManager owns. Unmanaged links
# are ignored by wait-online too, so it covers both. This is how wlu2u2 already behaves --
# nothing matches it, so networkd reports it unmanaged and leaves it to NM.
#
# The 10- prefix matters. networkd applies the FIRST matching .network in lexicographic
# order across all its directories, so this has to sort ahead of 80-wired.network.

[Match]
Type=ether
Name=!veth*

[Link]
Unmanaged=yes
